{{quote|"These are prisoners."<br/>"Yes. Where are you taking them?"<br/>"I am taking them to imprison them, in prison."|[[K-2SO]], questioned by a stormtrooper|quotestart=0|quoteend=0|<ref name="Rogue One">''[[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story]]''</ref>}}
[[File:DJ_in_Jail.jpg|thumb|right|300px|The [[slicer]] [[DJ]] in prison on Cantonica.]]
A '''prison''', also known as a '''detention block''' or a '''jail''', was a place where individuals were [[Prisoner|incarcerated]], including specialized buildings or entire [[planet]]s. Most [[The galaxy|galactic]] governments including the [[Galactic Republic]], the [[Galactic Empire]] and the [[New Republic]] maintained prisons to detain [[crime lord|criminals]], political dissenters or individuals deemed too dangerous to be allowed into society. Some prisons took the form of [[Factory|factories]] where the prisoners worked during their sentences; this was known as a '''work camp''', '''penal work camp''' or a '''prison factory'''. Others, intended for the offenders of the most serious crimes, were known as a '''supermax prison'''.

==History==
===Old and High Republic eras===
The [[Galactic Republic]] operated a number of prisons around [[the galaxy]], including the [[Republic Correctional Facility]] on the [[planet]] [[Pipyyr]],<ref name="Cataclysm">''[[The High Republic: Cataclysm]]''</ref> the [[Citadel]] on [[Lola Sayu]]<ref name="TC">{{TCW|The Citadel (episode)}}</ref> which was built in [[522 BBY]]<ref name="Databank">{{Databank|the-citadel|The Citadel}}</ref> with help from the [[Jedi Order]]<ref name="BMF 75">{{BuildFalconCite|75|Guide to the Galaxy}}</ref> to contain rogue [[Jedi]]<ref name="TC" /> and a [[Starlight Beacon detention center|detention center]] on the [[Starlight Beacon]].<ref name="First Duty">{{InsiderCite|issue1=201|issue2=202|Starlight: First Duty}}</ref> At the same time, the Jedi Order had its own [[Jedi Temple Detention Center|highly secure prison]] inside the [[Imperial Palace|Jedi Temple]] on the capital [[planet]] [[Coruscant]], which they used to contain [[Sith]]<ref name="NoP">''[[Nexus of Power]]''</ref> and other [[Dark side of the Force|Dark-siders]].<ref name="CL">[[Star Wars: Complete Locations (2016)|''Star Wars: Complete Locations'']]</ref>

===Clone Wars era===
At some point, the Jedi established the [[Sason Temple]]<ref name="Aphra 33">[[Doctor Aphra (2020) 33|''Doctor Aphra'' (2020) 33]]</ref> which was used to contain a [[Starweird]].<ref name="Aphra 34">[[Doctor Aphra (2020) 34|''Doctor Aphra'' (2020) 34]]</ref> With the eruption of the [[Clone Wars]], the combating factions of the Republic and the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]] expanded upon their already existing prison systems to detain newly arrested enemies.<ref name="TC" /> The Republic operated a prison specifically for high-status Separatist [[officer]]s inside the [[Imperial Inspectorate HQ|Republic Center for Military Operations]]<ref name="Trivia">{{SW|url=series/clone-wars/the-jedi-who-knew-too-much-trivia-gallery|text="The Jedi Who Knew Too Much" Trivia Gallery}}</ref> as well as the high-security [[Republic Judiciary Central Detention Center]], which was used to detain common criminals.<ref name="Deception">{{TCW|Deception}}</ref>

The Jedi Order lost control of the Citadel, which was taken over by the Separatists when they [[Capture of Lola Sayu|conquered Lola Sayu]].<ref name="TC" /> Besides the newly-acquired Citadel, the Confederacy also operated the [[space station]] prisons [[Starlag XIX]] and [[Sunspot Prison|Sunspot]], the [[Unreal City]] private prison,<ref name="Collapse">''[[Collapse of the Republic]]''</ref> the [[Spire (Stygeon Prime)|Spire]] fortress on [[Stygeon Prime]],<ref name="Son of Dathomir 1">[[Darth Maul — Son of Dathomir 1|''Darth Maul — Son of Dathomir'' 1]]</ref> and a [[Dooku's prison|top-secret detention wing]] in [[Dooku]]'s [[Castle Serenno]], which he used to keep the Jedi [[Quinlan Vos]].<ref name="Dark Disciple">''[[Dark Disciple]]''</ref>

===Imperial Era===
[[File:ArrthEnoPrisonComplex-2015StarWarsAnnual1.png|thumb|right|200px|The [[Arrth-Eno Prison Complex]] on Coruscant.]]
Following the restructuring of the Republic into the [[Galactic Empire]], the new government inherited many of the Republic's old prisons, including the one on the Center for Military Operations<ref name="Empire">{{TOTE|Devoted}}</ref> and the Judiciary Detention Center.<ref name="BMF 67">{{BuildFalconCite|67|Guide to the Galaxy}}</ref> By [[3 BBY]],<ref name="Legacy date">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates "[[Legacy (episode)|Legacy]]" to [[3 BBY]].</ref> there were thousands of Imperial prisons in [[the galaxy]],<ref name="Legacy">{{Rebels|Legacy (episode)}}</ref> including the Spire fortress on Stygeon Prime,<ref name="BMF 73">{{BuildFalconCite|73|Guide to the Galaxy}}</ref> and the [[Arrth-Eno Prison Complex|Arrth-Eno Custodial Complex]]<ref name="Annual 1">[[Star Wars Annual (2015) 1|''Star Wars Annual'' (2015) 1]]</ref> on the Imperial [[capital]] planet<ref name="UltimateSW">''[[Ultimate Star Wars]]''</ref> Coruscant.<ref name="Annual 1" /> The [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station|Death Star]] had a [[Detention Block AA-23|detention block]] where [[Governor]] [[Wilhuff Tarkin]] held [[Princess]] [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]] until she was [[Rescue of Princess Leia|rescued]] by [[Luke Skywalker]], [[Han Solo]], and [[Chewbacca]].<ref name="ANH">{{Film|IV}}</ref> The Empire also maintained a secret prison known as [[The Crypt (prison)|the Crypt]] on the outer reaches of the [[Anoat system]].<ref name="Uprising">''[[Star Wars: Uprising]]''</ref>

The Empire also maintained a vast number of penal work camps, such as the [[Narkina 5 Imperial Prison Complex|labor camp]]<ref name="Narkina 5">{{Andor|Narkina 5 (episode)}}</ref> on the [[moon]]<ref name="Audio description">{{Andor|Narkina 5 (episode)}} {{AD|Disney+}}</ref> [[Narkina 5]],<ref name="Narkina 5" /> the [[Delrian]] Prison Planet, the [[Oovo Four detention center]]<ref name="Rise">''[[Star Wars: The Rise and Fall of the Galactic Empire]]''</ref>&mdash;which was guarded by [[Firespray-31-class patrol and attack craft|''Firespray''-31-class patrol and attack craft]],<ref name="Absolutely Everything You Need to Know">''[[Star Wars: Absolutely Everything You Need to Know]]''</ref>&mdash;the [[Imperial Detention Center & Labor Camp LEG-817]]<ref name="Rebel Rising">''[[Rebel Rising]]''</ref> and the [[Jubilar]]. Prisons intended for the offenders of [[Class One Offense]]s, the most serious under the [[Imperial Legal Code]], were known as supermax.<ref name="Rise" />

===New Republic Era===
Following the end of the [[Galactic Civil War]], the victorious [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]] restructured itself into the [[New Republic]] and took over many Imperial facilities including the Delrian prison and Oovo Four. The New republic also operated other facilities such as the [[Karthon Chop Fields]].<ref name="Chapter 14">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 14: The Tragedy}}</ref>

The [[Canto Bight police headquarters]] was home to the largest jail on [[Cantonica]].<ref name="TLJ VD">''[[Star Wars: The Last Jedi: The Visual Dictionary]]''</ref>

